From 0bd70678674b64d3ffd1ecd78643abf6a49e3f72 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tyler Baker <tyler.baker@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 11:22:51 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] arm64: dts: qcom: qrb2210-arduino-imola: keep the RTC
 offset in RTCInfo

The PM4125 RTC counter is read-only to the application processor on the
UNO Q (the SPMI arbiter rejects the RTC_RW write with -EPERM), so the
time can only be set as an offset to the counter, and the board has no
nvmem cell for one. The board boots through UEFI firmware, which keeps
the offset in the RTCInfo variable. Describe that, so Linux reads the
time the firmware's SetTime() stored.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Tyler Baker <tyler.baker@oss.qualcomm.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/qrb2210-arduino-imola-base.dts | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/qrb2210-arduino-imola-base.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/qrb2210-arduino-imola-base.dts
index 34d62c832..0153fd3f8 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/qrb2210-arduino-imola-base.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/qrb2210-arduino-imola-base.dts
@@ -319,6 +319,10 @@ &mdss_dsi0_phy {
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+&pm4125_rtc {
+	qcom,uefi-rtc-info;
+};
+
 &pm4125_vbus {
 	regulator-min-microamp = <500000>;
 	regulator-max-microamp = <500000>;
-- 
